1
00:00:01,580 --> 00:00:02,300
Don't worry, Alexandra.

2
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:03,900
We'll find the owner.

3
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:05,600
How, Robbie?

4
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:07,400
Let me think.

5
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:08,600
Gemma, sit.

6
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:09,600
Good Gemma.

7
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:10,900
Give me your paw.

8
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:12,500
Good Gemma.

9
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:13,300
This dog is well trained.

10
00:00:13,300 --> 00:00:15,600
She likes you, too.

11
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:17,600
So how are we going to find the owners?

12
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:21,000
With a little help from the ASPCA,

13
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,400
the American Society for the Prevention of Cruelty to Animals.

14
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:25,800
They're the ones.

15
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:27,500
We once found a cat.

16
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:29,000
She was caught in the branches of our tree.

17
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:31,400
And Dad called the ASPCA.

18
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:32,800
They came and solved the problem.

19
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:38,900
Robbie, let's call them.

20
00:00:38,900 --> 00:00:46,600
Let me see -- ASPCA...

21
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:47,100
Here it is.

22
00:00:47,100 --> 00:00:57,780
ASPCA Animal Shelter.

23
00:00:57,780 --> 00:01:08,700
555-7700.

24
00:01:08,700 --> 00:01:10,800
Hello, ASPCA.

25
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:13,280
Hello, my name is Robbie Stewart.

26
00:01:13,280 --> 00:01:15,800
I have a lost dog I'd like to bring to you.

27
00:01:15,800 --> 00:01:16,800
How late are you open?

28
00:01:16,800 --> 00:01:19,000
We're open till nine P.M.

29
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:19,500
Thank you.

30
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:20,980
I'll bring the dog over by nine.

31
00:01:20,980 --> 00:01:22,000
Thanks.

32
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:23,300
Bye.

33
00:01:23,300 --> 00:01:23,500
Thanks.

34
00:01:23,300 --> 00:01:32,600
Good-bye.

35
00:01:32,600 --> 00:01:33,300
They're still open?

36
00:01:33,300 --> 00:01:35,200
They're open until nine o'clock.

37
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:36,900
We have two and a half hours.

38
00:01:36,900 --> 00:01:38,190
Let's take Gemma by there now.

39
00:01:38,190 --> 00:01:41,100
They'll find the owner.

40
00:01:41,100 --> 00:01:42,600
I hope so.

41
00:01:42,600 --> 00:01:46,000
I'm so sad to see this little dog without her family.

42
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:48,600
I'm sure they'll find the owner.

43
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:51,600
But if they don't, I'll adopt her.

44
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:55,200
She's so cute.

45
00:01:55,200 --> 00:01:58,400
Look at those eyes.

46
00:01:58,400 --> 00:01:59,100
She's hard to resist.

47
00:01:59,100 --> 00:02:03,300
Don't you just love her?

48
00:02:03,300 --> 00:02:05,400
I'd like to keep her, too.

49
00:02:05,400 --> 00:02:06,700
But I'll be going home to Greece

50
00:02:06,700 --> 00:02:09,600
at the end of the semester.

51
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:15,400
She just wants love and affection.

52
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:15,600
Come on, Robbie.

53
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:17,500
Let's get her to the animal shelter,

54
00:02:17,500 --> 00:02:20,800
so they can find her owners quickly.

55
00:02:20,800 --> 00:02:22,000
Don't worry, Gemma.

56
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:23,600
We'll get you home.

57
00:02:23,600 --> 00:02:26,200
It's not easy being away from home.

58
00:02:26,200 --> 00:02:27,500
Come on, poochie.

59
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:30,400
Atta girl!

60
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:31,400
Let's go.

61
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:56,790
We're off to the animal shelter.

62
00:02:56,790 --> 00:02:57,800
Your name?

63
00:02:57,800 --> 00:02:59,200
Robbie Stewart.

64
00:02:59,200 --> 00:03:01,700
And this is Alexandra Pappas.

65
00:03:01,700 --> 00:03:06,500
Your name will do, Mr. Stewart.

66
00:03:06,500 --> 00:03:10,800
Your address?

67
00:03:10,800 --> 00:03:14,600
46 Linden street, Riverdale.

68
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:16,600
Where did you find the dog?

69
00:03:16,600 --> 00:03:17,800
She found us.

70
00:03:17,800 --> 00:03:19,700
You tried calling the number on the collar?

71
00:03:19,700 --> 00:03:23,300
Yes, but the number's no longer in service.

72
00:03:23,300 --> 00:03:25,600
And there's no address on the dog tag?

73
00:03:25,600 --> 00:03:27,900
There's no other information.

74
00:03:27,900 --> 00:03:29,700
No ID number.

75
00:03:29,700 --> 00:03:33,200
Without that, it's hard.

76
00:03:33,200 --> 00:03:35,800
You will try to find the dog's owner.

77
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:38,900
Oh, we'll try, believe me.

78
00:03:38,900 --> 00:03:41,090
And if you don't?

79
00:03:41,090 --> 00:03:42,900
Yes?

80
00:03:42,900 --> 00:03:47,100
If you don't ... can I ... can I adopt the dog?

81
00:03:47,100 --> 00:03:48,200
Why, yes.

82
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:50,900
If the owners don't claim the dog in forty-eight hours,

83
00:03:50,900 --> 00:03:52,900
then you can apply for adoption.

84
00:03:52,900 --> 00:03:54,100
How do I do that?

85
00:03:54,100 --> 00:03:55,600
You really want to?

86
00:03:55,600 --> 00:03:57,400
Yes, I'm serious.

87
00:03:57,400 --> 00:03:59,200
If no one comes to claim Gemma,

88
00:03:59,200 --> 00:04:01,200
I'd like to adopt her.

89
00:04:01,200 --> 00:04:04,200
It's not difficult.
